{
  "source": "Extracted from draw.io desktop 31.3.2 (app.asar: stencils/*.xml, js/diagramly/sidebar/Sidebar-*.js) and rendered to PNG to confirm each icon. Nothing here is guessed.",
  "usage": "A style string is built from the cloud's styleTemplate with the service's fields substituted. Container styles are groupStylePrefix + the container's suffix, except where a full style is given.",
  "derivation": {
    "namingRule": "A stencil file declares shapes as <shape name=\"Elastic Load Balancing\">. mxStencilRegistry addresses them lowercased with spaces replaced by underscores, prefixed by the stencil file's root name: mxgraph.aws4.elastic_load_balancing. AWS uses the service name, not the marketing name: route_53 not route53, elastic_file_system not efs.",
    "verify": [
      "1. Grep the shipped stencil file, definitive and offline: npx --yes @electron/asar extract-file /Applications/draw.io.app/Contents/Resources/app.asar drawio/src/main/webapp/stencils/aws4.xml, then grep -o '<shape[^>]*name=\"[^\"]*\"' aws4.xml | sed 's/.*name=\"//;s/\"//' | tr ' ' '_' | tr 'A-Z' 'a-z' | sort -u. Same pattern for stencils/gcp3.xml and stencils/gcp/*.xml. For Azure list asset paths instead: npx --yes @electron/asar list ... | grep '^/drawio/src/main/webapp/img/lib/azure2/'.",
      "2. Render it and look: drawio -x -f png -o probe.png --page-index 1 --scale 2 probe.drawio. A bad resIcon is a plain coloured square, a bad Azure image path is a broken-image placeholder, a bad shape is a plain rectangle. All three exit 0.",
      "3. Cross-check Sidebar-AWS4.js / Sidebar-Azure2.js / Sidebar-GCP3.js for the intended colour and size as well as the name."
    ],
    "doNot": "Do not trust blog posts or guessed icon names. AWS renamed many stencils between the aws3/aws4/aws4b generations and Sidebar-AWS4b.js reuses the mxgraph.aws4 prefix with different colours."
  },
  "clouds": {
    "aws": {
      "notes": "Stencil based and fully name addressable: 1038 stencils. resourceIcon is a JS shape that fills a square in fillColor and draws the stencil named by resIcon inside it tinted with strokeColor, so strokeColor is the glyph colour (#ffffff for the official look) and fillColor is the tile. If resIcon names a stencil that does not exist the draw is simply skipped: a blank coloured square, no warning, exit 0. Shape libraries do not need enabling in the UI, stencils lazy load on first reference.",
      "styleTemplate": "sketch=0;outlineConnect=0;fontColor=#000000;fillColor=<FILL_COLOR>;strokeColor=#ffffff;dashed=0;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;verticalAlign=top;align=center;html=1;fontSize=12;fontStyle=0;aspect=fixed;shape=mxgraph.aws4.resourceIcon;resIcon=<RES_ICON>;",
